    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "This is an advanced topic. If you are just starting out with AOP, you can safely skip it until later."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "note"
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "By default, there is a single instance of each aspect within the application context. AspectJ calls this the singleton instantiation model. It is possible to define aspects with alternate lifecycles. Spring supports AspectJ’s "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "perthis"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "pertarget"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "pertypewithin"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " instantiation models; "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "percflow"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "percflowbelow"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " are not currently supported."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "You can declare a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "perthis"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " aspect by specifying a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "perthis"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " clause in the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Aspect"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation. Consider the following example:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@Aspect(\"perthis(execution(* com.xyz..service.*.*(..)))\")\npublic class MyAspect {\n\n\tprivate int someState;\n\n\t@Before(\"execution(* com.xyz..service.*.*(..))\")\n\tpublic void recordServiceUsage() {\n\t\t// ...\n\t}\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Java"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "@Aspect(\"perthis(execution(* com.xyz..service.*.*(..)))\")\nclass MyAspect {\n\n\tprivate val someState: Int = 0\n\n\t@Before(\"execution(* com.xyz..service.*.*(..))\")\n\tfun recordServiceUsage() {\n\t\t// ...\n\t}\n}"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "kotlin",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Kotlin"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "example",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In the preceding example, the effect of the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "perthis"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " clause is that one aspect instance is created for each unique service object that performs a business service (each unique object bound to "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "this"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " at join points matched by the pointcut expression). The aspect instance is created the first time that a method is invoked on the service object. The aspect goes out of scope when the service object goes out of scope. Before the aspect instance is created, none of the advice within it runs. As soon as the aspect instance has been created, the advice declared within it runs at matched join points, but only when the service object is the one with which this aspect is associated. See the AspectJ Programming Guide for more information on "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "per"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " clauses."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "pertarget"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " instantiation model works in exactly the same way as "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "perthis"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", but it creates one aspect instance for each unique target object at matched join points."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
